      "statusChangeID": "5d49ca20c05a7269067748ec",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "We have no intent of reverting the behavior of viseme resetting for lipsync, as the previous behavior was incorrect.\n\nThe intended method by which you use the \"sil\" and default states of the avatar are as such:\n\n\"sil\" - used when the microphone is active, but no audio is sent.\n\nDefault Avatar State - Used when there is no microphone activity.\n\nIdeally these should be (almost) the same, unless the intent is to have \"speaking, but in-between words\" blend shape unique. The previously implemented behavior was a bug. VRChat expects that the \"neutral\" state of any avatar does not have any speaking shapes enabled.\n\nIf you require an open mouth or etc while modeling, it is considered \"best practice\" that you keep a blend shape/shape key/pose available that poses your avatar in an appropriate manner for texture baking.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
