      ],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": "5d49ca20c05a7269067748ee",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5d424747f6752471dd1bf1e0",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}:\n\nThe VRChat team is setting the \"correct\" and \"intended\" behavior. I don't think that's a valid reason to close the thread as that's the only access we have to convince the team otherwise.\n\nSo this is the change as I understand it.\nPros to the viseme behavior change:\n  * It's now \"intended\" behavior.\n  * You can now have two unique silence blendshapes.\nCons to the viseme behavior change:\n  * Some avatars now have an open mouth while silent.\n\nIt seems really simple to implement all the pros and none of the cons by just adding an additional silence blendshape for people to hook up.\n\nAs for what's \"intended\", nothing's stopping the VRChat team from intending for the silence shape to be exactly the same as the Basis shape. You can intend that and still trigger the silence shape during silence.\nThey're the same shape after all!",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-08-01T01:58:31.560Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I use the sil blendshape to close the mouth of my models. With the recent VRChat update this functionality is removed.\n\nThe silence blendshape is important to any workflow that involves baking normals, since you typically want the mouth open during baking. \n\nI believe it would be trivial to trigger the silence blendshape during silence, and prevent breaking a bunch of avatars in the process.\n\nYour team is setting the conventions for avatar creation for everyone, and I believe that making the silence blendshape only trigger *sometimes* during silence is another unnecessary gotcha that creators will run into!\n\n(Alternatively just phasing out the silence blendshape entirely would make sense, you could automatically generate the shapekey for it right before upload. Though this would still leave old avatars broken.)",
